       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for an adult is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use.\n- A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot. That's true even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I can add that to the order note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
